### :returns: Two raised to the power `me`.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} when the result is NaN; {NumericOverflowError} on ±inf.
routine D32.exp2!() -> D32
  var r = me.exp2_unchecked()
  if r.is_finite()
    return r
  if r.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

### 2^me via libm double, raw IEEE: may return ±inf or NaN. Never crashes.
### :returns: Two raised to the power `me`, possibly non-finite.
routine D32.exp2_unchecked() -> D32
  return dd_to_d32(x: d32_to_dd(x: me).exp2())

